# Host crontab fragment for rpi-homeserver — generic jobs only, personal ones go in rpi-services.
#
# Not installed on its own: scripts/setup/install-crontab.sh merges both repos' fragments and
# apply.sh runs it on every deploy, so committing a change here applies it. Editing the live
# crontab with `crontab -e` is overwritten on the next deploy.
#
# What each script does: docs/architecture.md, "The scripts". The media, zram and disk numbers, and
# the tracker read-then-act pair, used to be five lines here and are now the pi-metrics and
# tracker-control services, scraped instead of pushed.

# Self-heal net for the deploy. The webhook handles pushes; this restarts anything that died and
# covers pushes that arrived while the Pi or the tunnel was down.
*/30 * * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/deploy/apply.sh >> /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/apply.log 2>&1

# Being retired, commented out on 2026-08-24. The script stays until it is decided whether anything
# replaces it; see PENDING.md. 05:00 and not 02:00 was because Plex holds 02:00-05:00 for its own
# maintenance and both land on the same platters (docs/lifecycle.md).
#0 5 * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/ops/cutoff-search.sh >> /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/cutoff-search.log 2>&1

0 4 * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/ops/backup.sh >> /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/backup.log 2>&1

# Dead man's switch, so someone outside notices within minutes if the Pi goes dark. No-op unless
# HEALTHCHECK_URL is set. See docs/alerting.md.
* * * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/ops/heartbeat.sh

# A minute is Oracle's own measured rate: exactly one launch call gets through per ~60s however
# hard you ask, so anything faster only raises the refusal count. Exits for good once the instance
# exists, so this is safe to leave forever. One summary line an hour, not one per run.
* * * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/ops/oci-hunt.py >> /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/oci-hunt.log 2>&1

# Prowlarr backs a failed indexer off for up to 24h, so an hour of the ISP blocking a site would
# otherwise cost a day of it being unusable. Probes the site first, never searches.
8,23,38,53 * * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/ops/indexer-retry.py >> /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/indexer-retry.log 2>&1

# Parked 2026-08-24: qbit-manage owns deletion, and two deleters with different rules is worse than
# either alone. Uncommenting this needs the qbit-manage share_limits groups paused. See PENDING.md.
#20 * * * * /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/scripts/trackers/seed-cleanup.py >> /home/raspi/rpi-homeserver/seed-cleanup.log 2>&1
